WEBVTT

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:02.610
Bari-bari...

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.660
...and I’m Assistant Kikuna.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.160
And today,
I’m here to assist Bari-chan.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.250
Bari-chan,
glad to be working with you!

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.130
Now then,
here on Bari Channel,

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.630
we’ll delve into the strange, strange
world of Pokémon and...

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.090
Bari-bari

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.090
...vigorously...

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.300
...investigate its secrets!

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.680
The theme for our memorable
first episode will be...

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.850
Bari-chan...

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.640
I haven’t said what it is yet.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.850
The first episode’s theme
is the following:

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.060
The Sakuragi Institute’s
Seven Mysteries.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.730
This is the Sakuragi Institute,

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.900
and we’ll showcase some of the
strange things that happen here.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.530
Bari-chan,
do the thing!

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.580
These are the Sakuragi Institute’s
Seven Mysteries!

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.040
Bari-chan,
any of these catch your eye?

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.630
Then today we’ll vigorously investigate
the Eevee that doesn’t evolve!

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.630
bari-bari

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.400
By the way, Bari-chan...

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.570
If we’re going to be reporting about Eevee,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.900
then naturally,
you must know all about Eevee, right?

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.870
And so, let’s begin with this!

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.240
Eevee Quiz

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:05.580
We’ll have you take a quiz on Eevee right now!

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.250
Everyone at home watching Bari Channel,
you should give it a try, too!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.550
Bari-chan, are you ready?

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:17.510
Then...
The Eevee quiz starts! V!

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.640
Which one is Eevee?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.060
What type is Eevee?

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.070
What Pokémon is Eevee?

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.910
How many evolutions does Eevee have?

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.080
Which Eevee is female?

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.420
What about Eevee is unstable?

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.000
Which one is taller?

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:57.800
Which one is heavier?

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.100
And it’s over!

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.220
Good work, Bari-chan!

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:10.020
With that, we’ve gone over
the basics of Eevee.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:13.400
Evolution is always on your mind
when thinking about Eevee.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:18.610
And that’s precisely why Koharu’s
Eevee that doesn’t evolve...

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.990
Hmm...
...is a mystery, indeed.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:24.660
So, to begin with,
what exactly <i>is</i> Pokémon evolution?

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.460
When Pokémon evolve, their appearances
and capabilities change greatly.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:33.800
Pokémon evolve in many different ways.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:38.970
There are even Pokémon which evolve
differently in different environments.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.680
Eevee has eight possible evolutions.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:47.180
That’s the highest amount
out of any known Pokémon.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:52.980
It’s said to be influenced by its surroundings
more easily than other Pokémon.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:57.440
Which is why it’s called
the Evolution Pokémon.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.950
Wait... Huh?

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:02.620
Hey, Bari-chan!
Were you listening?

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.830
I guess it was a bit too hard for you.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:12.000
Then, why don’t we actually
take a look at this Eevee that doesn’t evolve?

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.460
Well then, Bari-chan...
Take it away!

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:23.390
This is from just before
Koharu met Eevee.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:26.140
How come you haven’t
caught any Pokémon, Koharu?

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.850
Maybe I won’t.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:31.100
You won’t?! Why?

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:37.320
People make it out like I <i>have</i> to catch Pokémon
just because I’m a professor’s daughter.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.190
It doesn’t feel right.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:42.070
Being a
Pokémon professor’s daughter

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:45.160
colored how people
thought about her.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.530
She’s only ten.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.950
It’s no surprise
she can’t decide on her future.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:58.960
Miss!

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.050
What is it? Koharu?

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.850
Ah, uh, um, dad’s, uh, pachi...

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:09.310
Oh! Well, hurry back!

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.390
Wanpachi!

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.020
What’s wrong?

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.800
Like a scene from a fairy tale,

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:45.800
Koharu and Eevee
had a fateful encounter.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:49.310
They both look like they
fell in love at first sight!

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.060
That Eevee...

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:55.100
...had escaped from
a nearby laboratory,

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.650
and before long,
it was time for them to say goodbye.

00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:01.730
We’ve caused you
so much trouble.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:02.990
We’ll be off then.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:28.970
Eevee?!

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:45.030
This Eevee
really loves Koharu, huh?

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.780
It appears so.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:52.030
She’s a pretty mysterious Eevee.
She won’t evolve whatever we try.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:55.790
She won’t evolve into
any of the eight Pokémon?

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:56.960
Right.

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:05.420
Eevee have unstable genes in general,
so maybe that one’s genes are more unstable than most.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:10.050
Or perhaps... Maybe she’s hesitant,
unable to decide what path she should take.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.430
Hesitant...

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.730
Though that’s not a
very scientific perspective.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:17.100
Hey, Koharu...

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:20.600
If you wouldn’t mind,
do you think you could look after Eevee?

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:21.690
Huh?

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.900
You want to stay
with Koharu, don’t you?

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:29.240
Eevee...

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.620
If you say it’s okay...!

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.370
Thank you.

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:38.790
Koharu, who doesn’t know
what she wants to be...

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:41.920
...and Eevee,
who can’t decide which path to take.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.550
They’re very alike.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:50.130
Also, there’s more to this Eevee
than not evolving,

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.470
it has another mysterious trait as well.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.350
Take a look at this.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:07.190
Wanpachi! Eevee! Spark!

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:19.250
And that’s not all.

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:20.750
Everyone, look out!

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:25.500
Showers!
Use Hydro Pump!

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:40.850
Do... Do you want to fire
a Hydro Pump?

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.480
Eevee! Hydro Pump!

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:53.240
Eevee used Hydro Pump?!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.580
You did it!

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.460
Was that... Copycat?

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:15.050
The Copycat
that the man mentioned...

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:18.810
...is a move that copies
other Pokémon’s moves.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:21.020
But Koharu’s Eevee...

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:25.060
...only seems to copy moves
of the types of its own evolutions

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.810
Rather than “work experience,”

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:29.900
it’s enjoying its own unique
“evolution experience.”

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:34.990
As for this Eevee,
what does Koharu think about her?

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:37.740
She copies her evolutions’ moves?

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:39.830
That’s a real mysterious Eevee.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.870
Bari-chan, don’t get all confused!

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:47.710
The one wearing the kimono is Koharu.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:50.920
And this is Haruhi,
who looks just like Koharu.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.050
It’s confusing,
but hang in there!

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:55.050
With that settled,
let’s continue!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.300
That’s a real mysterious Eevee.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:01.220
Still, despite copying them,
she doesn’t evolve.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:07.650
Eevee have unstable genes in general, but they said
that maybe her genes are more unstable than most.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:09.690
Interesting...

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:11.650
And with her being like that...

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:16.530
That’s exactly why I want to
let her choose her own path herself.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:19.240
And so we’re learning
about lots of things together.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.580
I really get it!

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:23.160
You think just like I do!

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:28.750
These two, they evolved into Eefee
and Blacky on their own.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.590
Really?

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:34.260
Eefee, who’s strong in the day.
Blacky, who’s strong at night.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:40.300
The pair of them make up for each other’s flaws,
and support each other.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.560
Make up for each other’s flaws...

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.140
And support each other...

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:48.650
And humans and humans,
or humans and Pokémon can do the same.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:52.650
Nobody in the whole world’s
perfect all by their own.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:55.950
But by making up for each other’s flaws,
and supporting each other,

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:59.280
everybody gets to live life
a little easier.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:04.290
That’s what I feel,
seein’ how Eefee and Blacky are.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:07.460
Oh, she sounds so grown up...

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:08.830
For Pokémon Trainers,

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.290
it doesn’t matter if you’re
a child or an adult.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.590
By the way, Bari-chan...

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:17.760
Do you remember how many
kinds of evolutions Eevee has?

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:23.260
So close!
The answer was 8 kinds!

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:28.600
But Koharu and Eevee’s future
doesn’t just have eight paths.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:35.400
This is what happened the first time
Koharu and Eevee went to Alola.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.530
Um, Suiren...

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.700
It’s Koharu, right?

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:45.950
With the Eevee.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:46.830
Yeah!

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:49.830
You see...

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.590
I wanted to ask if you could
tell me about your Eevee.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:55.210
Sure!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:01.050
Hey, Suiren.
What are you going to evolve Sandy into?

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.550
Evolve?

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:07.640
Eevee and I have come across
lots of her evolutions.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:11.440
But I still don’t know...

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:15.860
...which of the eight
Eevee wants to evolve into.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:19.950
One more choice.
The Eevee path.

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:20.700
Huh?

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:24.030
Staying an Eevee.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.660
Like Satoshi’s Pikachu.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.830
Satoshi’s Pikachu?

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:35.210
I get it!
So Eevee have nine paths, not just eight!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:37.960
Lots of possibilities!

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.430
Lots of...
Possibilities!

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:42.590
Yeah!

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:46.680
Not evolving
and just staying an Eevee...

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.680
...is another possible future.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:54.190
And with that, we’re one step closer
to solving the Seven Mysteries!

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:57.820
Through her adventures with Eevee...

00:13:57.820 --> 00:14:01.030
Koharu’s world keeps on expanding!

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:05.740
What answer will
Koharu and Eevee arrive at?

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.950
Look forward to the next episode!

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:23.680
And... we’re off!

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:26.140
Today, You’re the Speed Star Radio!

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:32.980
I am your companion,
the guide for all of your journeys, Mr. Narra!

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:35.980
Life is full of up and downs,
and so are Pokémon!

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:39.980
And I hope to give you all a Helping Hand
as you Tackle your daily troubles!

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:43.530
Today, You’re the Star—
The Speed Star!

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:46.910
Oh, a new program started.

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:51.700
Yet again, thank you for the messages
you’ve sent in this week.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:59.210
Today, I’ll be starting off with a message
from Star Name “Daddy’s A Lonely Ball Lately”!

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:02.550
“Hello, Mr. Narra!”

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:04.090
Oh, hello!

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:08.470
“My daughter, who turned ten,
recently caught her first Pokémon.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.310
“It feels like they’re always
spending time together,

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:15.520
“and I’m glad that she’s found
such a wonderful partner.”

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:18.400
That is certainly worth celebrating.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:22.110
“She was never very proactive,

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:25.820
“and it feels like now
the Pokémon is encouraging her.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:28.070
“The other day...”

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.160
I’m back!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.460
I’m back, Wanpachi.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:38.210
Come on out, Eevee.

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:45.720
Welcome back, Koharu.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:47.260
I’m back, Dad.

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:49.220
Can you come here a moment?

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.520
Welcome back, Koharu.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.100
Nice timing!

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.190
What is it?

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:03.110
Hey! Have you been
finding fossils <i>enchanting?</i>

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:05.280
Apparently he has a request for you.

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:07.200
About investigating fossils!

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:09.820
In the Wild Area! The Wild Area!

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.160
Over in Galar?

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:12.910
<i>Indeeding!</i>

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:17.500
You can find rare fossils in Galar,
according to a rumor I heard.

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.170
I’ll do it!

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:20.880
Me, too!

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:25.380
I can meet lots of Pokémon
in the Wild Area! Right, Aceburn?!

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:28.380
What will you do, Koharu?

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:30.800
I have school, so...

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:34.720
You want to go?

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:44.480
Dad, I want to go too!

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:51.240
“With her Pokémon, she went
all the way to Galar for the first time,

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:54.370
“and had all kinds of experiences there.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:59.710
“She even got to witness fossils being restored,
and had a very satisfying day out,”

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:04.550
So, how was it?

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:07.050
Great! I had so much fun!

00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:10.510
I hope I can go again sometime!
Don’t you agree, Eevee?

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:14.180
All right!
Let’s write that report together!

00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:20.060
Well, they say kids grow up
at Lightning Speed.

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.600
And what’s wrong with that?

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:24.190
So how come
you’re “A Lonely Ball,” hmm?

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.940
Ehem...

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.570
“Without me even being there,

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:33.320
“when I see she’s growing up
by leaps and bounds,

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:36.910
“as her father,
I’m a bit of a lonely ball”

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:40.080
Oh, I get it now.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:43.330
“As she grows,
her worries have grown too.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:47.590
“Should I be reaching out to her,
or just watching over her?

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:52.720
“Just like my daughter,
I’m unsure what I should do.”

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:56.470
Hmm... I see.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:18:01.480
To everyone listening, if you have any opinions
or thoughts, don’t hesitate to send them in.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:04.150
Now then,
I have a song for you...

00:18:09.530 --> 00:18:13.030
...and that was “1, 2, 3.”

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:15.660
Erm... And we’ve already
received some messages.

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:19.450
Star Name
“Nervousçoise.”

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:20.950
“Hello, Mr. Narra.”

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.540
Oh, hello!

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.960
“I know a girl who’s very similar,

00:18:24.960 --> 00:18:27.380
“so I simply had to send in an e-mail.

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:29.130
Oh, thank you for that.

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:31.050
“Even if adults don’t reach out to them,

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:35.180
“sometimes children can still
find answers on their own.”

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:39.010
Koharu, what do
your mom and dad do?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:41.430
My mother’s an illustrator,

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:43.560
and my father researches Pokémon.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:46.230
Ooh! He’s a Pokémon Professor?

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:47.360
Yeah.

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:53.320
But I don’t like when people assume
I’m going to be a professor just because he is.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:57.200
At one point, I was panicking.
I was trying to think of something I wanted to do.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:03.080
Then I met Eevee,
and realized I don’t need to rush it.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.870
Eevee?

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:08.040
She’s a bit unique.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:11.630
It’s like she still doesn’t want to decide
what to evolve into.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:15.510
So she copies the moves of other Pokémon,
and tries out all kinds of things.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:16.340
Oh!

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:19.600
So earlier she was copying
Pochama’s move!

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:20.510
Yeah.

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.390
She seems to really enjoy that.

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:29.310
So I thought that it would be fine for me to hesitate
and just enjoy trying new things, too.

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:31.900
Ah, I see.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:36.070
My Pochama decided on his own
not to evolve.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:36.820
Huh?

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:42.200
He seems to want to stay by my side
as a Pochama forever.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:46.580
At the time, I wasn’t sure
that was really a good idea.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:51.550
But since then,
I’ve gotten a lot closer to Pochama.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:53.960
So you’ll be fine, just fine!

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:57.550
Thinking really hard about it
for a long time, then going “Eureka!”...

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:00.510
That’s how the greatest
dreams are born, I bet.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:04.390
Yeah!

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:09.810
Right, right! Dad shouldn’t butt in,
is that what you’re saying?

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.860
Harsh!

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:15.110
Next up, Star Name
“Yellow Lover.”

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:17.530
“Hello, Mr. Narra.”

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:18.450
Hello!

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:21.910
“I also know a wonderful girl
who met Pokémon,

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:25.120
“and began trying all kinds of things!

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:28.920
“Her father is a Pokémon Professor,
and lately,

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:31.500
“even the way they handle Pokémon
is growing more similar.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:35.670
“There’s something so fascinating
about kids and their parents!”

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:37.720
I think they’re going home.

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:39.970
Back to Full Moon Island
and New Moon Island.

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:44.140
So Darkrai was searching
for the wounded Cresselia.

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:47.180
I thought they were enemies...

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:50.480
But maybe they’ve actually
been looking after one another.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:53.650
Darkrai gives everyone
nightmares.

00:20:53.650 --> 00:21:00.200
But it can’t control that power,
so it always ends up hated and alone...

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:06.750
Maybe Cresselia lives on Full Moon Island
because it doesn’t want Darkrai to be lonely...

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:11.540
That’s amazing, Koharu!
You really understand how Pokémon feel!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:15.800
If we face each other earnestly,
people and Pokémon...

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:18.220
...can truly understand
one another...

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:23.470
Eevee.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.680
You know,
we might not be Pokémon,

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:33.360
but humans can evolve
bit by bit, too.

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:35.190
And I’m not just talking about kids.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:36.070
Dads can, too.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:40.240
Now then, here’s a song to go
with your coffee break...

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:44.490
After the song is the super popular
Eevee Fortunes corner!

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:09.450
This week’s Eevee Fortunes! V!

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:14.160
Pick your favorite Pokémon
out of these nine!

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:16.370
Oh... I can’t decide!

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:17.880
First up...

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:19.460
Super Happy!

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:21.880
If you picked Eefee...

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:24.050
You might just glimpse the future!

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:27.300
Your happy item
is a couples’ necklace!

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:29.470
Next up...

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:31.470
Super Lucky!

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:33.770
If you picked Nymphia...

00:23:33.770 --> 00:23:36.480
Everyone’s going to
fall in love with you!

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:38.980
Your lucky item is a ribbon!

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:44.650
And, this week’s Super Veevee is...

00:23:41.780 --> 00:23:45.490
Super Veevee

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:52.490
Every day, you won’t forget about Eevee!
You’ll have happy times ahead!

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:47.860
If you picked Eevee...

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:52.790
You won’t be able to forget about Eevee,
and you’re bound to have happy days ahead!

00:23:52.490 --> 00:24:00.420
[Good news] Eevee appears next episode!

00:23:52.790 --> 00:23:55.080
And I have good news for you!

00:23:55.080 --> 00:23:58.380
Eevee appears in next week’s
Pocket Monsters!

00:23:58.380 --> 00:24:00.420
What’ll it be about...?

00:24:02.090 --> 00:24:04.460
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:05.800
Go!

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:11.890
Oh, man! The more I think about Eevee evolving,
the less I seem to understand...

00:24:12.890 --> 00:24:15.520
Koharu, why don’t we
go camping this weekend?

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:15.890
Huh?

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:17.690
There’s something
I’d like to show you.

00:24:17.690 --> 00:24:19.020
Show me something?
What is it?

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:20.650
You’ll find out
when the day comes!

00:24:20.650 --> 00:24:23.650
What could it be...?
Now I really want to know!

00:24:24.360 --> 00:24:26.240
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:24:26.240 --> 00:24:29.320
Koharu and Eevee,
The Possibilities Are Endless!
